<BaseLayout title="Startup Product & Engineering Help — Matthew Cochran" description="Focused product, architecture, AI, and delivery engagements for startup teams at consequential scaling and technical inflection points.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Startup engagements / Selective" title="Clarity at consequential inflection points." description="Focused help for technical founders when product direction, architecture, AI integration, delivery mechanics, or organizational scale have become material company risks." aside="Bounded engagements · Decision-grade output · Hands-on depth" />
  <section class="section shell engagement-fit"><div><p class="kicker">Best fit</p><h2>When the next decision is expensive to reverse.</h2></div><div class="signal-list"><article><span>01</span><h3>Scale readiness</h3><p>Architecture, operating practices, and product focus are creating drag before the next hiring or growth phase.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Product and platform repair</h3><p>A flagship or underperforming product needs a credible technical and delivery path—not another abstract assessment.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Governed AI adoption</h3><p>The team needs useful AI capabilities with explicit boundaries, evaluation, security, approval, and operational control.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Program recovery</h3><p>Critical work lacks dependency clarity, delivery control, decision rights, or a trustworthy critical path.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="methodology"><div class="method-grid"></div><div class="shell method-content"><p class="kicker">The engagement</p><h2>Diagnose. Decide. Leave the team stronger.</h2><p>Work is time-bound and outcome-oriented. It can include evidence gathering, product and architecture analysis, failure-mode and threat analysis, critical-path planning, implementation prototypes, and a sequenced decision blueprint.</p><div class="method-steps"><span>Evidence</span><i>→</i><span>Risk</span><i>→</i><span>Options</span><i>→</i><span>Decision</span><i>→</i><span>Execution path</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="section shell offer-grid"><article><p class="kicker">Scale Readiness Diagnostic</p><h2>A focused 4–6 week engagement.</h2><p>For Series A SaaS teams with real growth pressure, typically 10–50 engineers, and authority to act on the findings.</p></article><div><h3>Decision artifacts</h3><ul><li>Structural Scaling Map</li><li>Market Resonance Risk Map</li><li>Scale Readiness Blueprint</li><li>Sequenced priorities across product, architecture, team, and delivery</li></ul><h3>Clear boundaries</h3><p>Not staff augmentation, an indefinite fractional retainer, or a workshop without concrete output. Engagements typically start at $25k.</p><a class="button primary" href="/snapshot/">Take the readiness snapshot →</a></div></section>
